__baseline__.text:
React 18 StrictMode → dev-only double-invoke mount effects (mount→cleanup→mount) intentional. Purpose: surface missing/broken cleanup (leaks, stale subscriptions) before prod.

Not a bug. Prod build: runs once.

Fix if breaking something: write proper cleanup fn, don't treat effect as "runs once ever."

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const sub = subscribe();
  return () => sub.unsubscribe(); // cleanup — required for StrictMode safety
}, []);
```

Opt out only via removing `<React.StrictMode>` — not recommended, hides real bugs.

__terse__.text:
React 18 StrictMode dev-only behavior. Mount → unmount → remount, on purpose. Surfaces effects w/o proper cleanup.

Why: future concurrent features may mount/unmount components repeatedly (offscreen, fast refresh). React tests your cleanup now vs bite you later.

Not bug. Fix root cause: every `useEffect` w/ subscription/timer/listener needs matching cleanup return.

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(tick, 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(id); // cleanup required
}, []);
```

Prod build: runs once, no double-invoke. `StrictMode` wrapper only culprit — remove it and effect runs once even in dev, but don't (masks bugs).

